              definition="#cd92da3c-dabc-4352-8406-10793ad92c60" value="Open the shutdown circuit when hard braking coincides for longer than half a second with tractive current corresponding to five kilowatts delivered to motors at nominal battery voltage. Also open the shutdown circuit for any open or short on a BSPD sensor input. The symbolic current threshold is 5000 W divided by nominal battery voltage; the voltage, hard-braking criterion and actual circuit design remain unresolved. Global trip latching/manual-reset behavior belongs to the separate shutdown slice."/>
