          <ownedRequirements xsi:type="Requirements:Requirement" id="19ff6d4d-cc9f-47be-9375-b0105ab160d0"
              ReqIFIdentifier="FSAE2027:VP:obligation:STEEL" ReqIFLongName="FSAE2027:VP Meet all steel minima and prescribed calculation properties"
              requirementType="#f8e4778c-4fd3-4570-94cf-86b53014d474" ReqIFText="For each steel class satisfy all four simultaneous minima (inertia mm^4, area mm^2, outside diameter/square width mm, wall mm): A=(11320,173,25.0,2.0), B=(8509,114,25.0,1.2), C=(6695,91,25.0,1.2), D=(18015,126,35.0,1.2). Example round tubes are A:1.0 in x 0.095 in or 25 x 2.5 mm; B:1.0 in x 0.065 in or 25.4 x 1.6 mm; C:1.0 in x 0.049 in or 25.4 x 1.2 mm; D:1.375 in x 0.049 in or 35 x 1.2 mm. Examples are not additional compulsory sizes. For any steel in SES calculations use continuous/nonwelded E=200 GPa(29000 ksi), Sy=305 MPa(44.2 ksi), Su=365 MPa(52.9 ksi); for discontinuous/welded joint calculations use Sy=180 MPa(26 ksi), Su=300 MPa(43.5 ksi). If welded reinforcement is needed, prove equivalence of the welded tube plus reinforcement to the original nonwelded tube. Welded inserts have thicker walls and smaller outer diameter/square side than that original tube and are welded at both ends. Do not mechanically alter structural weld shapes.">
            <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="dc2d2adb-8ea7-493b-904d-b8ea93f55002"
                definition="#f28516c8-9d0f-4e03-b0f2-cefc6667b433" value="FSAE-2027-V1"/>
