          <ownedRequirements xsi:type="Requirements:Requirement" id="53e9a872-24c7-418a-97f0-fb8f06b881ed"
              ReqIFIdentifier="FSAE2027:VP:obligation:ALUMINUM" ReqIFLongName="FSAE2027:VP Retain conditional aluminum construction and evidence"
              requirementType="#f8e4778c-4fd3-4570-94cf-86b53014d474" ReqIFText="Use aluminum tubing only in applications permitted by the application table. The SES includes material identity/properties with purchase, shipping or donation evidence, equivalence calculations against the steel minima/nonwelded reference in yield/ultimate bending, buckling, tension, buckling modulus and energy dissipation, plus manufacturing process details. Aluminum wall minima are 2.0 mm nonwelded and 3.0 mm welded. SES nonwelded 6061-T6 values are E=69 GPa(10000 ksi), Sy=240 MPa(34.8 ksi), Su=290 MPa(42.1 ksi); welded values Sy=115 MPa(16.7 ksi), Su=175 MPa(25.4 ksi). Use the alloy's as-welded equivalent yield strength unless detailed proof establishes correct solution treatment/artificial aging and absence of later manufacturing heating. Postweld strengthening evidence identifies the facility, process and fixturing.">
