          <ownedRequirements xsi:type="Requirements:Requirement" id="6c21c97d-2bb3-40d9-ab5e-50a692d2632f"
              ReqIFIdentifier="FSAE2027:VP:obligation:AIP" ReqIFLongName="FSAE2027:VP Retain AIP material and attachment alternatives"
              requirementType="#f8e4778c-4fd3-4570-94cf-86b53014d474" ReqIFText="Choose a solid steel AIP at least 1.5 mm thick, solid aluminum at least 4.0 mm thick, or a composite meeting F.8.3. For welding, the profile reaches or exceeds the bulkhead tube centerline on every side; for bolting/bonding/laminating it reaches or exceeds the complete outer bulkhead periphery. Document direct attachment in SES. Weld lengths are at least 25 mm with interrupted weld/space ratio at least 1:1. Bolting uses at least eight critical fasteners at least 8 mm or 5/16 in diameter, with bolt centers at least 50 mm apart, and 15 kN pullout/bending capacity per attachment. Tearout is 15 kN per bolt or total mounting tearout exceeds the F.8.5.3.b attenuator attachment strength. Bonding requires no bulkhead openings, bonding over the AIP's entire surface and shear/peel strengths strictly above 120 kN. Laminating places the AIP ahead of the outer bulkhead skin, encloses it fully and provides shear capability strictly above 120 kN.">
            <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="4c88bb1e-0f59-4fff-b3dd-18581c77ed18"
                definition="#f28516c8-9d0f-4e03-b0f2-cefc6667b433" value="FSAE-2027-V1"/>
