          <ownedRequirements xsi:type="Requirements:Requirement" id="f1b5c1b8-4b36-4a9c-b917-83d666a13d47"
              ReqIFIdentifier="FSAE2027:VP:obligation:IA-EVIDENCE" ReqIFLongName="FSAE2027:VP Plan the applicable impact report, fixture, conduct and analysis"
              requirementType="#f8e4778c-4fd3-4570-94cf-86b53014d474" ReqIFText="For standard IA, omit test-data submission but include all other section requirements, photos of the actual IA and evidence against its specification (supplier receipt/packing slip is allowed). Nonstandard IAD includes functional test data, energy/deceleration calculations, test schematic and photos annotated with pre/post heights; IA testing is valid only one competition year. During tests use intended IA-to-AIP attachment and a representative chassis section/fixture equivalent in strength/stiffness to baseline bulkhead, not a solid bulkhead-shaped block. Leave at least 50 mm fixture clearance behind AIP; permanent deflection anywhere is at most 25 mm beyond its pretest position. Composite IA requires dynamic testing; other constructions may use dynamic or quasi-static. Dynamic tests occur at a dedicated facility under professional/faculty supervision, not a team-built dynamic apparatus; quasi-static tests may use university facilities with the source's due-care advice retained. Calculate average dynamic deceleration from raw unfiltered data. If peaks exceed 40 g, the permitted filter is CFC 60(100 Hz) underSAE J211 or a 100 Hz third-order low-pass Butterworth(-3dB at 100 Hz).">
            <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="a9b6049f-d8c8-49df-bc70-a892c5cb3c56"
                definition="#f28516c8-9d0f-4e03-b0f2-cefc6667b433" value="FSAE-2027-V1"/>
