          <ownedRequirements xsi:type="Requirements:Requirement" id="ff0ca743-c63e-410c-b5ea-89ba83f39ef2"
              ReqIFIdentifier="FSAE2027:VP:obligation:HARNESS" ReqIFLongName="FSAE2027:VP Retain certified harness and posture-dependent alternatives"
              requirementType="#f8e4778c-4fd3-4570-94cf-86b53014d474" ReqIFText="Select a 5-,6- or 7-point harness certified to SFI 16.1, SFI 16.5 orFIA 8853/2016. Keep original labels/specification/expiration, use within the labeled expiration year (expiry on/before 31December of the competition calendar year is permitted), keep new/like-new condition without wear/cuts/chafing, follow manufacturer installation/threading and never modify supplied hardware. Five points are two lap/two shoulder/one antisubmarine belt; six use two lap/two shoulder/two leg or antisubmarine belts; seven add a negative-g/Z belt. Template seat-back angle at most 30 degrees is upright, strictly above 30 degrees is reclined; the chest-to-groin line follows shoulder belts to release buckle in side view. Reclined requires 6/7 points and either quick-adjust antisubmarine belts or two installed sets. All lap belts have tilt-lock quick adjusters; pull-up over pull-down is recommended. Use separate over-shoulder straps, neverY straps; H configuration is allowed.">
            <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="4d1a438b-fdcb-4da2-a93a-624b73dccc63"
                definition="#f28516c8-9d0f-4e03-b0f2-cefc6667b433" value="FSAE-2027-V1"/>
