        <ownedRequirements xsi:type="Requirements:Folder" id="1d7aebaa-47df-42eb-b182-70a9b089d212"
            ReqIFIdentifier="FSAE2027:SUB:DES" ReqIFLongName="FSAE2027:SUB DES Design Event documents (Design Briefing, Design Spec Sheet, Vehicle Drawings) - S.4.2 to S.4.5, with S.4.6 to S.4.9 event-day evidence"
            requirementType="#f8e4778c-4fd3-4570-94cf-86b53014d474" ReqIFText="The Design Event (150 of the 325 static points, S.1:p003, S.4.10.1) needs three documents uploaded before the event: a Design Briefing (PDF, on the official event template), a Design Spec Sheet (XLSX, on the provided format) and three-view Vehicle Drawings (PDF, no template; layout set by S.4.4.1). See S.4.2.1, S.4.3, S.4.4, S.4.5 and Table PS-1 rows p011-p013. The Design Judges review them before the event and use them to sort teams into design groups (S.4.2.2). Judges may also give part of the Design score to the documents themselves (S.4.9.2). Each document is uploaded as a single file into the team's own account on the Event Website by the due date posted there; the briefing and spec sheet must use the official templates with their format left unchanged (PS.1.1.1, PS.2.1, PS.2.2.1-PS.2.2.4). A file in the wrong form or format counts as Not Submitted (PS.1.2.5). A late upload costs 20 points for each day late in the 'Other' penalty group. A document still missing after the cancellation date means removal from the Design event with zero points (S.4.2.3, PS.3.2.1, PS.3.2.2, Table PS-2:p004, S.4.10.3). At the event the judges score from these documents, a conversation with team members and their own look over the finished car (S.4.9.1). The car must arrive fully built, and its tractive battery pack must already have passed inspection (S.4.6.2, IN.5.3). Rulebook S.4.3.2 hands the briefing's detailed content and per-topic slide limits to the template. Public FSAE Michigan guidance from fsaeonline.com describes the spec sheet as a two-page subsystem specification spreadsheet. It describes the briefing as a technical design-review document that judges scan across subsystems. Neither official template is reproduced here, so the briefing sections and spec-sheet fields below are derived from the rulebook's numeric limits and that public guidance. Confirm them against the 2027 templates on the Event Website. Model state: the S.4, PS.2.2, IN.5.3 and Table PS-1 design rows are in the model, but nothing in S.4 is traced to a design element yet. The model holds no numeric property values.">
          <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="929a13f0-2aeb-4789-9c78-52b8f0e68357"
              definition="#2accec6a-53af-443b-ac05-920a9e2f77d8" value="FSAE2027:submissions-v1"/>
          <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="352508cf-05cd-44cf-a76a-76c35eb8aaa1"
              definition="#f28516c8-9d0f-4e03-b0f2-cefc6667b433" value="FSAE-2027-V1"/>
          <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="655101ca-6fb5-4b1b-bf2a-a6f25e0a8614"
              definition="#24357558-2768-408a-b07d-be62178d9e15" value="f71df5552e341dab1b58f1ff47212e7281953d66b9c41833de8347560913ed0e"/>
          <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="fe165194-2483-4f0c-a45d-a71a1de238ce"
              definition="#abd36e5a-eaa7-47b8-8c54-0e0cdbabce20" value="DES"/>
          <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="782e33c6-130f-4c5f-b630-78a5ac5f158b"
              definition="#8418021d-4a12-4509-ab78-bf1394b884d6" value="[&quot;S.1 (static event points: Design 150)&quot;,&quot;S.4.1.1-S.4.1.3 (what the judges assess: engineering effort, meeting the design goals at good value, and how bought-in items were chosen and applied)&quot;,&quot;S.4.2.1 (three Design Documents required)&quot;,&quot;S.4.2.2 (judges review the documents before the event and use them to group teams)&quot;,&quot;S.4.2.3 (late penalties come from section PS)&quot;,&quot;S.4.2.4 (documents that are not a serious effort can lead to exclusion or a lower score)&quot;,&quot;S.4.3.1-S.4.3.3 (Design Briefing must use the event template, which sets content areas and slide limits per topic)&quot;,&quot;S.4.4.1-S.4.4.2 (Vehicle Drawings: front, top and side line views, each on its own page, by hand or CAD)&quot;,&quot;S.4.5 (Design Spec Sheet on the provided format; ranges are allowed for values that will be tuned)&quot;,&quot;S.4.6.1-S.4.6.2 (full Inspection Approval is not needed before judging; car presented complete; EV battery pack must have passed inspection; unfinished cars are not judged; preparation faults can cost points)&quot;,&quot;S.4.7.1-S.4.7.2 (optional support material; space at the event may be limited)&quot;,&quot;S.4.8 (judging may run in rounds, such as a first round and then finals)&quot;,&quot;S.4.9.1-S.4.9.3 (judging inputs are the documents, a discussion and a vehicle inspection; points are deducted if the team cannot explain the car; score sheets are on the Event Website)&quot;,&quot;S.4.10.1-S.4.10.3 (0-150 points; penalties; excluded teams score zero)&quot;,&quot;PS.1.1.1-PS.1.1.2, PS.1.2.1-PS.1.2.6 (due date, cancellation date, late and not-submitted definitions including wrong format, days-late rounding)&quot;,&quot;PS.2.1, PS.2.2, PS.2.2.1-PS.2.2.4 (upload location, required templates from the Event Website, no format changes, one file per submission, PDF or XLSX)&quot;,&quot;PS.3.1.1-PS.3.1.4, PS.3.2.1-PS.3.2.3, PS.3.3.1 (team confirms its own upload, free replacement before the due date, revision deadlines, penalties, removal of entry for ignoring reviewer requests)&quot;,&quot;Table PS-1 rows FSAE-2027-V1:TABLE-PS-1:p011 (Design Briefing, PDF, template), p012 (Vehicle Drawings, PDF), p013 (Design Spec Sheet, XLSX, template), p014 (template note)&quot;,&quot;Table PS-2 row FSAE-2027-V1:TABLE-PS-2:p004 (Other group: daily late penalty; removal from Design with zero points if not submitted)&quot;,&quot;IN.5.3 (the tractive battery pack, fitted or loose, may not appear at a static event until its inspection is fully done)&quot;,&quot;Rules that bound Design Spec Sheet values: V.1.2 wheelbase minimum, V.1.3.1-V.1.3.2 track and rollover stability, ratio of smaller to larger track, V.1.4.1-V.1.4.2 ground clearance and lower side impact structure height, V.3.1.1 minimum wheel travel, V.4.1 minimum wheel diameter, V.4.3 tires, EV.3.3.1 80 kW energy-meter power cap, EV.3.3.2 600 V DC voltage cap, EV.3.3.3 no regeneration from 0 to 5 km/h, EV.4.1-EV.4.2 motors and controller, EV.5 energy storage, T.3 brakes, T.7 aero devices, F.3-F.8 chassis materials, structure and front protection&quot;]"/>
          <ownedAttributes xsi:type="Requirements:StringValueAttribute" id="d6bb8842-6665-4214-b4ff-6de61d3bcc8e"
              definition="#80d1a35c-a9c8-40de-a65a-a8e64d29b2ab" value="PDF briefing, XLSX spec sheet, PDF drawings"/>
